{
    "unit_id": "english_v2",
    "unit_title": "中学英語 Vol.2 (応用編)",
    "order": 2,
    "chapters": [
        {
            "title": "1. 未来形と助動詞",
            "sections": [
                {
                    "title": "未来を表す表現",
                    "content_blocks": [
                        {
                            "type": "introduction",
                            "text": "「〜するつもり」「〜でしょう」という未来のことを話すときは、will か be going to を使います。"
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "point",
                            "title": "will と be going to",
                            "content": "**will**\\n- その場で決めた意思、単純な未来\\n- I **will** help you.\\n\\n**be going to**\\n- 前から決めていた予定\\n- I **am going to** visit Kyoto next week."
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "example_problem",
                            "title": "例題1: 未来形",
                            "problem": "I visit Kyoto tomorrow. を未来の文に（予定として）。\\nI ( ) ( ) ( ) visit Kyoto tomorrow.",
                            "solution_steps": [
                                "予定なので be going to を使う",
                                "答え: **am going to**"
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "point",
                            "title": "助動詞",
                            "content": "**can**: 〜できる\\n**must**: 〜しなければならない\\n**may**: 〜してもよい、〜かもしれない\\n**should**: 〜すべき\\n\\n※ 助動詞の後は**動詞の原形**！"
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "example_problem",
                            "title": "例題2: 助動詞",
                            "problem": "You ( ) be quiet in the library.",
                            "solution_steps": [
                                "図書館では静かにしなければならない",
                                "答え: **must**"
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "exercise",
                            "problems": [
                                {
                                    "q": "He ( ) swim very fast. [できる]",
                                    "a": "can"
                                },
                                {
                                    "q": "It ( ) rain tomorrow. [かもしれない]",
                                    "a": "may"
                                },
                                {
                                    "q": "You ( ) study harder. [すべき]",
                                    "a": "should"
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "2. 不定詞と動名詞",
            "sections": [
                {
                    "title": "不定詞 (to + 動詞の原形)",
                    "content_blocks": [
                        {
                            "type": "point",
                            "title": "3つの用法",
                            "content": "1. **名詞的用法**: 〜すること\\n   - I like **to swim**.\\n2. **形容詞的用法**: 〜するための\\n   - I have a lot of books **to read**.\\n3. **副詞的用法**: 〜するために\\n   - I went there **to study**."
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "example_problem",
                            "title": "例題3: 不定詞",
                            "problem": "私は英語を勉強するためにここに来ました。\\n( came / here / I / English / study / to ).",
                            "solution_steps": [
                                "主語＋動詞: I came here",
                                "目的（副詞的用法）: to study English",
                                "答え: **I came here to study English.**"
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "title": "動名詞 (動詞+ing)",
                    "content_blocks": [
                        {
                            "type": "point",
                            "title": "動名詞の使い方",
                            "content": "動詞に **-ing** をつけて「〜すること」を表す。\\n- I enjoy **reading** books.\\n- **Swimming** is fun."
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "point",
                            "title": "不定詞と動名詞の使い分け",
                            "content": "**動名詞だけをとる動詞**: enjoy, finish, stop, mind など\\n**不定詞だけをとる動詞**: want, hope, decide など\\n**両方OK**: like, start, begin など"
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "example_problem",
                            "title": "例題4: 動名詞",
                            "problem": "He finished ( ) his homework.",
                            "solution_steps": [
                                "finish は動名詞のみをとる",
                                "答え: **doing**"
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "exercise",
                            "problems": [
                                {
                                    "q": "I want ( ) soccer. [play]",
                                    "a": "to play"
                                },
                                {
                                    "q": "She enjoys ( ) music. [listen]",
                                    "a": "listening"
                                },
                                {
                                    "q": "Stop ( ) so loud! [talk]",
                                    "a": "talking"
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "title": "3. 比較",
            "sections": [
                {
                    "title": "比較級と最上級",
                    "content_blocks": [
                        {
                            "type": "point",
                            "title": "比較の3つの形",
                            "content": "**原級**: as ~ as （同じくらい）\\n**比較級**: ~er than / more ~ than （より〜）\\n**最上級**: the ~est / the most ~ （最も〜）"
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "example_problem",
                            "title": "例題5: 比較",
                            "problem": "Ken is ( ) than Tom. [tall]",
                            "solution_steps": [
                                "比較級なので -er をつける",
                                "答え: **taller**"
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "type": "exercise",
                            "problems": [
                                {
                                    "q": "This flower is ( ) of all. [beautiful]",
                                    "a": "the most beautiful"
                                },
                                {
                                    "q": "He runs as ( ) as his brother.",
                                    "a": "fast"
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}